					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/carolynn-ivy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5070187); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5070187&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608149476" alt="carolynn ivy" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5070187)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/carolynn-ivy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5070187); return false;" >carolynn ivy</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608081907 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">16 Dec 2020 01:25</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4845805">
									

<p>I had trouble reading this at first because I don't think the tone behind some of the dialogue was clear to me the first time.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Dialogue&nbsp;tone</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The lines</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Rex: Yes. You're like if someone tried making a really shitty Little Mister.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>and</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Rex: Of course you don't understand. You're just a stupid little plastic failure of a children's product.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230;for example, read as stilted to me until I read a second time and imagined Rex as a dude who genuinely doesn't give a shit about Taste, beyond disgust. Imagining him just kinda muttering that second line while loading stuff into the cart really helped it feel more natural. But then lines like</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Rex: Indeed! Now, let's begin. It says here you are coated in ethylene glycol?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>and</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Rex: Do not press this further.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>are so formally phrased that it kind of breaks that dispassionate and condescending character. That contrast makes the dialogue feel difficult for me to emotionally follow.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>That aside, I enjoy the way you juxtapose the emotional abuse of a sentient being with its similarly unconcerned treatment under Foundation bureaucracy. It gives a sense of how little the Foundation cares about small-fry objects like Taste beyond being a means to some end. Personally I think Taste's abuse isn't particularly more interesting or emotionally engaging on its own than any other article in which a sentient SCP is cruelly treated, even though Taste's childlikeness does make it sting a <em>little.</em> It's those bureaucratic and cold emails that do it for me. I also like the subtle commentary on brand loyalism under capitalism, intentional or not. You'd think any dude mass-producing child-marketed and extremely dangerous anomalies would be given equal concern by the foundation regardless of brand, but.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;stupidly&nbsp;small&nbsp;nitpick</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The &quot;to do so&quot; in &quot;It is sentient and capable of speech, despite lacking the necessary organs to do so&quot; should be chopped.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Let me know if I'm reading that dialogue wrong.</p>

							</div>

								
